Z||000000||DaveL||08-16-2000||12:48 PM||||I'm convinved I have a problem with my TVC. The auto tranny on my 87 SE 2.5 DIS usually shifts perfectly. Occasionally though, the shifts are delayed until 3000 rpm or so. However, if I put the shifter in the second gear position, then shift to the 3rd gear position, it shifts!? My Haynes book only has illustrations for the 300 Throttle Body cable and adjustment. Mine has the model 700 Injector system, and the TVC looks different. There is a wheel near the injector where the throttle cable from the pedal connects, also the throttle Valve cable. This goes down to the throttle body and appears  to be attached by one bolt. In the middle of the cable, there are two tangs that seem to be some sort of connection. Any suggestions? Does anyone know if this type of cable requires adjustment?||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||08-16-2000||09:06 PM||||The TV cables are adjustable, but if most of the time it shifts ok, then it's probably another problem and not the TV cable. Check fluid level and consider changing it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-16-2000||09:13 PM||||Definatly check and consider a filter & fluid change. You could have some dirt in there moving around. There's a number of threads about how to do that. It's not hard just somewhat messy.<P>make sure the TV cable moves free. If it's binding then replace it. It's about the same procedure as the older one even tho the top end is diferant.||||reg||1
